      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-18394",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/31/31df5fe79f2aa8715321b6500474683a01732788e5fafc3300dfffc83c266893.png)\n\nConsider a box with width $x$, height $y$, and depth $z$, as shown above. The width of the box is three times its depth. Given that the box's volume is $54$ cubic units, what is the smallest possible surface area of the box? Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
